gluon_target.datei:
include 'bcm27xx.inc'

device('raspberrypi-4-model-b', 'rpi-4', {
	manifest_aliases = {
		-- from Gluon 2023.1 and older
		'raspberry-pi-4-model-b-rev-1.1',
		'raspberry-pi-4-model-b-rev-1.2', -- untested
		'raspberry-pi-4-model-b-rev-1.4', -- untested
		'raspberry-pi-4-model-b-rev-1.5', -- untested
	},
})

gluon_target.bcm27xx.inc:
-- We do not use the ext4 images, so we do not want to build them.
config('TARGET_ROOTFS_EXT4FS', false)

defaults {
	factory_ext = '.img.gz',
	sysupgrade_ext = '.img.gz',
}

deviwiki_2gb._text:
:{{ProductPage|https://www.raspberrypi.org/products/raspberry-pi-4-model-b}}

In addition to the $45 model with 2 GiB of RAM, a version with 4 GiB of RAM is available for $55 and a 1 GiB version is available for $35.

''Raspberry Pi 4 Model B'' and ''© Raspberry Pi 2018'' are silkscreened near the 40 pin GPIO connector.  ''FCC Made in the UK'' and ''HDMI'' are silkscreened near the micro HDMI ports.

